Chapter: SectionTitleKeywords

 A class or instance declaration begins its line. The words `class` and
 `instance` inside a section title, or anywhere else in prose the lexer
 keeps, declare nothing.

class Showable where
  to-text : a -> Text

instance Showable Integer where
  to-text (x) = integer-to-text x

Section: Notes (see instance Showable Text below)

  describe : Showable a => a -> Text
  describe (x) = "<" & to-text x & ">"

Section: More notes (the class Showable where it matters)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (describe 42)
  end
